# slug: ch04-parse
# source: chapters/ch04.tex:86 (approximate line of \begin{algorithm})
# caption: Recursive-descent parsing of Mini expressions with layered precedence.
# label: alg:ch04-parse
# require: token list T with a cursor at position P
# ensure: syntax tree for one expression with the cursor past its last token, or a syntax error
# keywords: INPUT/OUTPUT/REQUIRE/ENSURE/FOR/FORALL/WHILE/IF/ELSE/RETURN

REQUIRE token list T with a cursor at position P
ENSURE syntax tree for one expression with the cursor past its last token, or a syntax error
FUNCTION ParseExpr(T)
  set Left to the result of parsing one product
  WHILE the cursor shows an add or subtract operator DO
    consume the operator and parse the next product as Right
    set Left to a new node combining Left and Right
  END WHILE
  RETURN Left
END FUNCTION

